<title>UK: BT slips on regulatory worries, profit-taking.</title>
<headline>BT slips on regulatory worries, profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Telecommunications Plc were slightly lower on Wednesday amid profit-taking and regulatory worries despite news that BT had won a one billion telephone contract.</p>
<p>The shares were 1-1/2p lower at 368-1/2p by 1035 GMT in volume of 5-1/2 million shares.</p>
<p>&quot;There has been a bit of profit-taking after the euphoria,&quot; one dealer said, referring to news of a planned merger with U.S. long-distance telephone operator MCI.</p>
</text>
